# Context

## Why This Way
The README had grown into a feature-by-feature inventory that mixed
marketing, keystroke reference, and development status. New readers
could not tell what Margin does or reach a working review session
quickly.

The rewrite reorganizes the same facts around user tasks: write,
review, browse history, work beside an agent, and scope capture.
Detail moved to the existing guides (docs/source-editing.md,
docs/desk-links.md, examples/README.md) instead of living inline.

## Gotchas
- All file and asset references were verified to exist before
  committing; keep that check when editing the link list.
- The quick start now applies examples/after/*.md over examples/before
  and opens the TUI directly, so it must stay runnable as one Bash
  session (MARGIN_EXAMPLES/MARGIN_DEMO variables).
- The long "Development status" narrative was replaced by a short
  limitations list; to-do.json remains a snapshot that can lag.

## Related
- docs/README.md and docs/remaining-gaps-plan.md now carry the
  delivery-status detail removed here.
